ismail yosgot says he'll never celebrate  his birthday again  it was one day before his birthday in  april 2006 that his 21 year old son  haleed was murdered shot as he worked in  the family's internet cafe in the city  of castle  he was the ninth victim in a series of  racially motivated killings  mr yosgot gave evidence of the trial of  biata chapa who is accused of  involvement in the murders he said he  found his son in a pool of blood at the  internet cafe  for years the authorities wrongly  suspected the family and didn't  investigate a possible right-wing link  to the crime  scene one of the goals of this case is  to make clear the family was unfairly  suspected  they were spied on by an investigator  their telephone was tapped  even though mr yoskat told police the  only motive could be racism that the  family had nothing to do with it and  that the investigations were heading in  the wrong direction  one witness andreas t testified that he  had been in the internet cafe but that  he didn't see the murder and only read  about it later in the newspaper  andreas t attracted attention because he  worked for germany's domestic  intelligence agency at the time he said  his failure to come forward as a witness  was a mistake  he also expressed his sympathy to the  families of all the victims
 

